# Protocols and Ports for DevOps

## Introduction

In DevOps, servers, applications, cloud services, and CI/CD pipelines communicate using different network protocols. Understanding these protocols and their default port numbers is essential for deploying applications, configuring firewalls, troubleshooting connectivity, and securing infrastructure.

---

# Common DevOps Protocols and Ports

| Protocol         | Port    | Transport Protocol | Purpose                               | DevOps Use Case                                 |
| ---------------- | ------- | ------------------ | ------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------- |
| HTTP             | 80      | TCP                | Transfers web pages                   | Access web applications                         |
| HTTPS            | 443     | TCP                | Secure web communication              | Secure websites and APIs                        |
| SSH              | 22      | TCP                | Secure remote login                   | Connect to Linux servers and EC2 instances      |
| FTP              | 21      | TCP                | File transfer                         | Upload and download files                       |
| SFTP             | 22      | TCP                | Secure file transfer over SSH         | Secure deployment of application files          |
| DNS              | 53      | UDP/TCP            | Resolves domain names to IP addresses | Access websites and cloud services              |
| SMTP             | 25, 587 | TCP                | Send emails                           | Application email notifications                 |
| POP3             | 110     | TCP                | Receive emails                        | Email clients                                   |
| IMAP             | 143     | TCP                | Synchronize emails                    | Mail servers                                    |
| DHCP             | 67, 68  | UDP                | Automatically assigns IP addresses    | Network configuration                           |
| Telnet           | 23      | TCP                | Remote login (not secure)             | Legacy systems                                  |
| NTP              | 123     | UDP                | Synchronizes system time              | Keep servers synchronized                       |
| LDAP             | 389     | TCP/UDP            | Directory services                    | User authentication                             |
| LDAPS            | 636     | TCP                | Secure LDAP                           | Secure directory services                       |
| MySQL            | 3306    | TCP                | MySQL database connection             | Backend databases                               |
| PostgreSQL       | 5432    | TCP                | PostgreSQL database connection        | Application databases                           |
| MongoDB          | 27017   | TCP                | MongoDB database                      | NoSQL applications                              |
